WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.770
It's important to keep an eye on Joe Biden's
policy proposals because on the one hand,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.530
you have Donald Trump holding huge rallies
as if there's no pandemic, while insulting

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.599
Joe Biden saying Joe Biden is stupid, as he
did earlier this week.

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:14.809
And then, on the other hand, as a contract
contrast.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:18.279
You have Joe Biden actually proposing some
pretty interesting policies.

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:24.380
And one such policy that Joe Biden recently
released is a 10 percent tax penalty on companies

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.599
that move operations overseas.

00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:30.809
And then on the other side of that, a 10 percent
tax credit for companies that create jobs

00:00:30.809 --> 00:00:32.450
in the United States.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:38.540
I like the idea of Joe Biden rolling out more
economic policies, because if you're someone

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.860
who's voting on the big picture, right, you
you realize Donald Trump is a completely incompetent,

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.240
systemic threat to the United States and the
world.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.040
And he's made the country a global laughingstock.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.150
You may already be clear on I'm voting Biden
in November.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:01:00.810
There are people who, for one reason or another,
need some more specific economic justifications

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.160
to vote for Joe Biden.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.940
And one of those is that Joe Biden says he
will reverse some of the worst policies of

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:13.020
the Trump administration, which he believes
are loopholes that allow offshoring to take

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.389
place, despite Donald Trump claiming his entire
campaign entering his presidency, that he

00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:23.090
would be and has been great for the American
worker and for American business.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:30.170
It's impossible to ignore the reality that
Joe Biden on some of these issues is saying

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.429
he will achieve the exact same thing Donald
Trump promised to achieve when he was campaigning,

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:40.700
which is Joe Biden, much like Donald Trump
said in 2015, says he will revive American

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.789
manufacturing.

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:46.539
Joe Biden, much like Donald Trump campaigned
on in 2016, says he will create more American

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.369
jobs and bring some supply chains back to
the United States.

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:55.399
Of course, you will notice that the reason
Joe Biden is saying he will do those same

00:01:55.399 --> 00:01:59.439
things is Donald Trump promised to do them,
but failed to do so.

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:03.979
And Joe Biden's new proposal will target offshore
profits now and then.

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:09.619
This is going to bigger picture get added
into his plan to require corporations to pay

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:13.530
at least a 15 percent minimum tax on domestic
profits.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.840
As many of you know, even though we have a
corporate tax rate here in the United States

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.350
with no required minimum tax on corporations
the way individuals have.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:27.140
There's something called the alternative minimum
tax for individuals, meaning you can't use

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.260
deductions and loopholes to get down to not
owing anything.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.840
That in theory.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.300
That's the point of the alternative minimum
tax.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.120
Joe Biden is proposing something similar for
corporations.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:46.170
On the other side of this is you've got on
one side a 10 percent tax for offshoring and

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:51.380
then you have a 10 percent made in America
tax credit, which you would qualify for if

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:58.090
you, as a business owner, revitalize a closed
or almost closed facility in the United States.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.700
If you expand a facility, if you bring some
production back to the United States and there

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:09.020
will also be a 10 percent credit available
if you increase manufacturing wages, it has

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:14.090
to be based on pre corona virus has a baseline
up to 100 hundred thousand dollars.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.360
This is super interesting.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.570
Let me give you an example of how it works.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:23.300
You could conceivably have an employee earning
50000 dollars and you could say, I'm going

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:29.210
to give them a raise to sixty thousand dollars
on that 10000 dollar raise.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.660
Biden's proposal is the government will kick
you back 10 percent of it.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.170
So you give a ten thousand dollar raise.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.290
The government gives you a thousand dollar
tax credit.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.620
So you give someone ten thousand dollars.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.150
It only costs you nine.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.900
That's very, very interesting.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.260
And, you know, the macro economic impact needs
to be scored.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.740
But conceptually, it's very interesting.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:55.330
Now, I wonder how many of you are waiting
to see whether I will do this.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:04:00.420
I would be a hypocrite if I didn't point this
out when Joe Biden says it, because I sure

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.430
as hell pointed it out when Donald Trump said
it.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.180
All of the talk about bringing manufacturing
jobs back to the United States.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.510
A lot of these jobs are not coming back.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.510
Period.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.020
It doesn't matter if Donald Trump is president.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.710
It doesn't matter if Joe Biden is president.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:17.610
And, you know, a 10 percent credit here, a
10 percent tax there.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.910
It's not going to do it.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:24.080
And that is because the United States made
the decision implicitly decades ago that we

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.700
are going in the direction of being more of
a service based economy, more of a creative

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:33.940
economy, and outsourcing manufacturing to
places where it's cheaper, like China.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.570
That's the reality.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:40.389
And that's a global reality that's bigger
than 10 percent tax here, 10 percent credit

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:41.389
there.

00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:46.350
Now, that being said, if this incentive got
American companies to, for example, move a

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:50.530
call center back to the United States, that
is much more plausible.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:54.490
And I would find super interesting four for
me, one of the biggest.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:57.840
Service nightmares is when you're trying to
deal with something sensitive.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:04.340
For example, banking, payroll, airline tickets,
Internet security and customer service centers

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:10.290
are located in other parts of the country,
which is fine other than when you're dealing

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:14.490
with people that do not speak English at a
certain level of proficiency.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.030
That really affects customer service.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:19.650
And when you look at Internet service providers,
that offshore call centers, when you look

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:25.450
at airlines and all of these others consistently,
it destroys the customer experience.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.370
We've had recent Internet problems.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:32.110
Our Internet service providers tech support
is in another part of the world run by mediocre

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.110
English speakers.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.110
They're not bad people.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.540
They're no worse than Americans.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.510
But it is not a great customer service experience.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:43.670
At one point, the payroll company we used
to have had customer service overseas.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:48.010
It's not a great experience to be trying to
setup, you know, the proper tax deductions

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:51.730
for employees and to have someone where you
don't even know if their English level is

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.370
at a level of proficiency where they're getting
what you're trying to do.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:06:01.760
If this idea gets call centers back in the
United States, that would be super interesting

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.110
and it would be really good for a lot of companies.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:08.419
In any case, we're going to continue tracking
Joe Biden's proposals.

00:06:08.419 --> 00:06:09.740
This is an interesting one.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:13.680
Meanwhile, Donald Trump is doing rallies and
calling Joe Biden stupid.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.200
You decide which approach you prefer.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:15.220
I know which one I prefer.

